From 3745912327364e590fabcbcd342a9eb985fe82f7 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 7 Nov 2026 13:49:24 -0500
Subject: [PATCH 3/9] iommu: apple-dart: Keep the T6050 ANE DARTs for the cold
 ANE backend

The T6050 ANE DARTs are owned like the T8140 ones: the staged ANE backend
takes SID 0 only, after its own cold checks, and every inherited stream
stays as the boot loader left it. Treat "apple,t6050-ane-dart" as a cold
ANE DART: no reset, no global enable, no IRQ, and a refused probe when
the DART is locked or not the expected revision.

Assisted-by: LLM Claude
Signed-off-by: Rolando Trevino <rolotrealanis@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
index d39ee78d9d73..2c62a7350e4d 100644
--- a/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
+++ b/drivers/iommu/apple-dart.c
@@ -4199,7 +4199,8 @@ static int apple_dart_probe(struct platform_device *pdev)
 	dart->dev = dev;
 	dart->hw = of_device_get_match_data(dev);
 	dart->tunneled = tunneled;
-	dart->cold_ane = of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8140-ane-dart");
+	dart->cold_ane = of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8140-ane-dart") ||
+			 of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t6050-ane-dart");
 	if (dart->cold_ane && !IS_BUILTIN(CONFIG_APPLE_DART))
 		return -EOPNOTSUPP;
 	dart->per_stream = of_device_is_compatible(dev->of_node, "apple,t8140-dart") ||
